# vergeio_tenant_storage (Resource)

Allocates capacity from a storage tier to a tenant. `provisioned` is the quota in bytes and must be a whole number of GiB (a positive multiple of 1073741824). VergeOS floors non-aligned values, so the provider rejects them at plan time. Changing `tenant_id` or `tier` replaces the allocation. `tier` is the storage tier key (0 through 5 on a typical system).

